    "full_details": "Notices\nThe Scenario Event \"All Together! IF Kindergarten\" is back! Get the ★4 \"Kibaou\" Skill Record, stamps, and more!\nEVENT\n2026-04-15 17:00:00\n（JST/GMT+9）\nThe Scenario Event \"All Together! IF Kindergarten\" is back!\nThis event will carry over the following progress from the previous run:\n・Quest progression and rewards\n・Total Score and Score Rewards\n・Challenge rewards\n・Amount traded\n・Achievements and achievement progress\n* Previously deleted items such as \"Red Crayon\", \"Blue Crayon\" and \"Apple Gelatin\" will not be carried over.\nAlso, this event will be supported by Story Replay from now on.\nAfter fully completing the scenario quest, you can replay it via the dungeon NPC for the event.\nWhat is \"All Together! IF Kindergarten\"?\nAnother weird day has dawned.\nYou wake up from a nap to find a flustered 《Kibaou》...\nRewards\nGet the event-limited \"★4[Humorous Principal] Kibaou\" Skill Record, Memory Stamps, and more!\nGet up to 1000\n\"Arcana Gems\"\n, up to 100\n\"Awakening Star\"\n, up to 20\n\"Medal of Combat Arts\"\n, and up to 250\n\"Memoria Niter S\"\nfrom the event.\n\"Star Fragment\" may drop on certain difficulty levels!\nSkill Record\n★4[Humorous Principal] Kibaou\nSkill Name\nShadow Indemnity/Resentment\nAttack\n59\nDefense\n20\nHP\n1855\nSkill Effect\n[Shadow Indemnity 1] When you are cursed, dark element damage +25%./[Resentment] Adds Curse effect on yourself for 30 sec when you hit using Switch.\n*Evolving & Maximum Breakthrough\nMemory Stamp\nStamp Name\nStamp Displayed\nMORE DEBAN\nEvent-limited item\nIcon\nItem Name\nEffect\nApple Gelatin\nSnack time is the best!\nIncreases player's attack by 7% for 3 min.\nTrade \"Red Crayon\" for special items.\nTradable Item List\nAmount Needed\nTrade Limit\n★4[Humorous Principal] Kibaou\n400\n1\nMedal of Combat Arts\n300\n3\nAwakening Star\n20\n25\nMemoria Niter S\n500\n5\nTrade \"Blue Crayon\" for special items.\nTradable Item List\nAmount Needed\nTrade Limit\nArcana Gems×10\n20\n30\n★4[Humorous Principal] Kibaou\n400\n1\nMedal of Combat Arts\n300\n3\nAwakening Star\n20\n25\nMemoria Niter S\n500\n5\nTotal Score Reward\nYou'll earn a certain score by clearing the dungeon.\nScores earned in \"Starting Point\", \"Depth\", \"DANGER\" and \"Gaining Ground\", difficulties all count toward the\n\"Total Score Reward\"\n. Your rewards will be based on your score.\nThe score earned in \"Extreme\" difficulty is not added to the \"Total Score Reward\", but you will receive rewards based on your score.\nDungeon\nScore calculation\nMax Score\nStarting Point\nBasic Clear Bonus:74P＋Survival Bonus:1P per surviving player\n80\nDepth\nBasic Clear Bonus:170P＋Survival Bonus:5P per surviving player\n200\nDANGER\nBasic Clear Bonus:420P＋Survival Bonus:10P per surviving player\n480\nGaining Ground\nBasic Clear Bonus:1680P＋Survival Bonus:20P per surviving player\n1800\nExtreme\nBasic Clear Bonus:1000P＋Survival Bonus:20P per surviving player\n1120\n\"\nGaining Ground\n\"\nYou can get a high score in the \"\nGaining Ground\n\" difficulty bonus dungeon.\nYou can clear the \"\nGaining Ground\n\" one time per day.\nTake it on every day to get more total rewards!\nHigh difficulty \"\nExtreme\n\"\nThe high-difficulty dungeon \"\nExtreme\n\", has a recommended Total Power of 140,000. The boss has weaknesses that are different from those on other difficulty levels.\nThere will be Total Power restrictions for players who join Gaining Ground and Extreme difficulty Quick Parties.\nGaining Ground: Quick Party participation requirement - Total Power 40,000 or higher\nExtreme: Quick Party participation requirement - Total Power 60,000 or higher\nSpecial items that can be received from Total Score Rewards\n★4[Humorous Principal] Kibaou×9\nArcana Gems×600\nMemoria Niter S×200\nMedal of Combat Arts×9\nAwakening Star×35\nGreat Red Jewel×5\nGreat Green Jewel×5\nGreat Yellow Jewel×5\nGreat Blue Jewel×5\nSpecial items that can be received from \"Extreme\" Score Rewards\nMemoria Niter S×30\nMedal of Combat Arts×5\nAwakening Star×15\nGreat Yellow Jewel×5\nGreat Green Jewel×5\nGreat Blue Jewel×5\nGreat Red Jewel×5\nAchievement Rewards\nComplete the conditions and receive event-limited records and items from achievement rewards.\nRecord\nAchievement Requirements\nAchievement Rewards\nStrategy Team\nLet's collect a total of 2000 Red Crayons in the time period\nRevive Crystal×1\nIF Kindergarten\nLet's collect a total of 5000 Red Crayons in the time period\nRevive Crystal×1\nTons of Friends\nLet's collect a total of 2000 Blue Crayons in the time period\nRevive Crystal×1\nEvent Period\nStarts after the April 15, 2026 (Wed) maintenance and ends before the May 13, 2026 (Wed) maintenance.\nTrader Period\nStarts after the April 15, 2026 (Wed) maintenance and ends before the May 20, 2026 (Wed) maintenance.\nParticipation Requirements\nComplete the 1F Main Quest\nHow to Participate\nTalk to the \"Kibaou\" at the \"Teleport Gate Plaza\" to start the scenario quest.\nThere are 4 scenario quests. Clear them all to unlock the dungeon.\nStory Replay\nAfter completing the scenario quest, you can replay it via the dungeon NPC for the event.\nStory Replay is displayed beneath the dungeon.\nBoss Monster\n？？？\nDetails\nSkill Break with Slash Element.\nFor the Extreme difficulty, Skill Breaks can be performed with skills that are both \"Slash Element\" and \"Fire Element\".\nOnly specific parts will be vulnerable to attack at specific times.\nParts that can be attacked will display a color cursor.\nOn \"Extreme\" difficulties, the enemy uses a Seal Items debuff.\nWeakness\nSlash Element\nHoly Element\nWeakness\n* Only \"Extreme\" difficulty\nSlash Element\nFire Element\nStatus Ailments and Debuffs used\nStatus ailments \"Debility\" and \"Paralysis\"\nDebuff \"Decrease defense\" and \"Seal item\"\n* Skill Break: By completely lowering the Skill Break Gauge, the boss will be temporarily immobilized and all of its buff effects will be removed.\n* Debility: Lowers max HP with each hit (up to 99%).\nRecover using items like Cleansing Potions.\nImportant\nPlease check all Rewards in the game.\nIf you receive a stamp you already own, it will not have any effect when used.\nIf the ★4 Skill Records you acquire as rewards for this event have already reached their Limit Break max, they will be exchanged for \"Record Kit M\".\nAfter you clear the Gaining Ground dungeon once, you can't play it again until the limit resets at 4:00 (JST/UTC+9).\n\"Red Crayon\", \"Blue Crayon\", and \"Apple Gelatin\" will be deleted on May 20, 2026 (Wed) at 13:59 (JST/UTC+9).\nThere are no first or last attack bonuses on any difficulty.\nScenario quests cannot be attempted with an Assist Party.\nThe schedule may be subject to change without notice. Thank you for your understanding.\nGo to Notice List",
