    "full_details": "Notices\nScenario Event \"Heroine Destruction Rhapsody\" is back! Get limited-edition Skill Records, stamps, and more!\nEVENT\n2026-04-15 17:00:00\n（JST/GMT+9）\nThe Scenario Event \"Heroine Destruction Rhapsody\" is back!\nThis event will carry over the following progress from the previous run:\n・Quest progression and rewards\n・Total Score and Score Rewards\n・Challenge rewards\n・Amount traded\n・Achievements and achievement progress\n* Previously deleted items such as \"Blue Rose Tear\", \"Red Rose Tear\" and \"Soothing Bell\" will not be carried over.\nAlso, this event will be supported by Story Replay from now on.\nAfter fully completing the scenario quest, you can replay it via the dungeon NPC for the event.\nThe Scenario Event \"Heroine Destruction Rhapsody\"\nOne day, which should have been a peaceful day,\na single friend message suddenly arrives from 《Argo》.\nRewards\nGet the event-limited Skill Record ★3 [Goddess of Mayhem] Lisbeth and Memory Stamps!\nExchange the \"Blue Rose Tear\" and \"Red Rose Tear\" you obtain from the event at the exclusive Trader to get items.\nGet \"Red Rose Tear\" and exchange them for up to 300\n\"Arcana Gems\"\nat the Trader.\nGet up to 1,000\n\"Arcana Gems\"\n, up to 100\n\"Awakening Star\"\n, and up to 25\n\"Medal of Combat Arts\"\nfrom the entire event.\n\"Star Fragment\" may drop on certain difficulty levels!\nAssisting Character Eugeo\nObtain Blue Rose Badges from the Trader to unlock Assisting Character Eugeo from the achievement rewards.\nBlue Rose Badges can also be earned from the 85F main quest rewards.\nPlus, you can use Blue Rose Badges to get Friendship EXP for Eugeo.\nSkill Record\n★3[Goddess of Mayhem] Lisbeth\nSkill Name\nAdvance Trooper\nAttack\n30\nDefense\n32\nHP\n1850\nSkill Effect\n●[Advance Trooper 2] Attack +180\n*Evolving & Maximum Breakthrough\nMemory Stamp\nStamp Name\nStamp Displayed\nCleaning Maid\nShy Gentleman\nEvent-limited recovery item\nIcon\nItem Name\nEffect\nSoothing Bell\nBell that rings with a soothing tone.\nRecover party member's HP in the same field by 2000.\nTrade \"Blue Rose Tear\" for special items.\nTradable Item List\nAmount Needed\nTrade Limit\n★3[Goddess of Mayhem] Lisbeth\n400\n1\nBlue Rose Badge\n1\n1\nMemory Stamp 196\nUse to obtain the \"Shy Gentleman\" stamp.\n150\n1\nMedal of Combat Arts\n300\n5\nAwakening Star\n20\n30\nGreat Blue Jewel\n40\n5\nGreat Red Jewel\n40\n5\nGreat Green Jewel\n40\n5\nGreat Yellow Jewel\n40\n5\nTrade \"Red Rose Tear\" for special items.\nTradable Item List\nAmount Needed\nTrade Limit\nArcana Gems×10\n20\n30\n★3[Goddess of Mayhem] Lisbeth\n400\n1\nMedal of Combat Arts\n300\n5\nAwakening Star\n20\n20\nGreat Blue Jewel\n40\n5\nGreat Red Jewel\n40\n5\nGreat Green Jewel\n40\n5\nGreat Yellow Jewel\n40\n5\nTotal Score Reward\nYou'll earn a certain score by clearing the dungeon.\nScores earned in  count toward the\n\"Total Score Reward\"\n. Your rewards will be based on your score.\nThe score earned in \"Extreme\" difficulty is not added to the \"Total Score Reward\", but you will receive rewards based on your score.\nDungeon\nScore calculation\nMax Score\nStarting Point\nBasic Clear Bonus:74P＋Survival Bonus:1P per surviving player\n80\nDepth\nBasic Clear Bonus:170P＋Survival Bonus:5P per surviving player\n200\nDANGER\nBasic Clear Bonus:420P＋Survival Bonus:10P per surviving player\n480\nGaining Ground\nBasic Clear Bonus:2280P＋Survival Bonus:20P per surviving player\n2400\nExtreme\nBasic Clear Bonus:1000P＋Survival Bonus:20P per surviving player\n1120\n\"\nGaining Ground\n\"\nYou can get a high score in the \"\nGaining Ground\n\" difficulty bonus dungeon in this event.\nYou can clear the \"\nGaining Ground\n\" 1 time per day.\nTake it on every day to get more total rewards!\nHigh difficulty \"\nExtreme\n\"\nThe dungeon, \"\nExtreme\n\", has a recommended Total Power of 120,000. The boss has weaknesses that are different from those on other difficulty levels.\nThere will be Total Power restrictions for players who join Special and Extreme difficulty Quick Parties.\nSpecial: Quick Party participation requirement - Total Power 40,000 or higher\nExtreme: Quick Party participation requirement - Total Power 60,000 or higher\nSpecial items that can be received from Total Score Rewards\n★3[Goddess of Mayhem] Lisbeth×9\nArcana Gems×600\nMedal of Combat Arts×15\nAwakening Star×50\nGreat Red Jewel×5\nGreat Green Jewel×5\nGreat Yellow Jewel×5\nGreat Blue Jewel×5\nSpecial items that can be received from \"Extreme\" Score Rewards\nGreat Red Jewel×5\nGreat Green Jewel×5\nGreat Yellow Jewel×5\nGreat Blue Jewel×5\nAchievement Rewards\nComplete the conditions and receive event-limited records and items from achievement rewards.\nRecord\nAchievement Requirements\nAchievement Rewards\nHeroine Power!\nLet's collect a total of 2000 Blue Rose Tears in the time period\nRevive Crystal×1\nHeroine Destruction\nLet's collect a total of 5000 Blue Rose Tears in the time period\nRevive Crystal×1\nResolved Feelings\nLet's collect a total of 2000 Red Rose Tears in the time period\nRevive Crystal×1\nEvent Period\nStarts after the April 15, 2026 (Wed) maintenance and ends before the May 13, 2026 (Wed) maintenance.\nTrader Period\nStarts after the April 15, 2026 (Wed) maintenance and ends before the May 20, 2026 (Wed) maintenance.\nParticipation Requirements\nComplete the 1F Main Quest\nHow to Participate\nTalk to the \"April Fool 2022\" NPC at the \"Teleport Gate Plaza\" to start the scenario quest.\nThere are 6 scenario quests. Clear them all to unlock the dungeon.\nThe dungeons and some of the scenario quests have \"fields with unusable items\" where certain items cannot be used.\nStory Replay\nAfter completing the scenario quest, you can replay it via the dungeon NPC for the event.\nStory Replay is displayed beneath the dungeon.\nBoss Monster\nGlitter Harpy\nDetails\nIt appears in the dungeon difficulties \"Starting Point\" and \"Depth\".\nSkill Break with Thrust Element.\nWhen preparing the Skill Breakable attack, it gains a buff that reduces damage.\nWeakness\nThrust Element\nFire Element\nBuffs used\nBuff \"Reduces damage\"\nStatus Ailments used\nStatus ailments \"Poison\"\nThe Gleam Eyes\nDetails\nIt appears in the dungeon difficulties \"DANGER\", \"Gaining Ground\", and \"Extreme\".\nIt deals attacks that inflict the debuff \"Decrease Defense\" and remove buffs from the player.\nSkill Break with \"Thrust Element\".\nSkill Break with \"Slash Element\" in the \"Extreme\" difficulty.\nWhen preparing the Skill Breakable attack, it gains a buff that reduces damage.\nWeakness\nThrust Element\nFire Element\nWeakness\n* Only \"Extreme\"difficulty\nSlash Element\nDark Element\nBuffs used\nBuff \"Reduces damage\"\nDebuffs used\nDebuff \"Decrease defense\"\n* Skill Break: By completely lowering the Skill Break Gauge, the boss will be temporarily immobilized and all of its buff effects will be removed.\nImportant\nPlease check all Rewards in the game.\nThe specs of the boss monsters appearing in the game are different from the original monsters. See this announcement and in-game dungeon information for details.\nThe Assist Function is unlocked when you clear the 1F of Aincrad.\nIf you receive a stamp you already own, it will not have any effect when used.\nIf the ★3 Skill Records you acquire as rewards for this event have already reached their Limit Break max, they will be exchanged for \"Memoria Niter M\".\n\"Blue Rose Tear\", \"Red Rose Tear\" and \"Soothing Bell\" will be deleted on May 20, 2026 (Wed) at 13:59 (JST/UTC+9).\nAfter you clear the Gaining Ground dungeon once, you can't play it again until the limit resets at 4:00 (JST/UTC+9).\nThere are no first or last attack bonuses on any difficulty.\nScenario quests cannot be attempted with an Assist Party.\nThe schedule may be subject to change without notice. Thank you for your understanding.\nGo to Notice List",
