    "full_details": "Notices\nChapter 2 Aincrad 33F! Super rare Gale Integral Series 3rd level transformation unlocked!\nUPDATE\n2025-02-27 17:00:00\n（JST/GMT+9）\nMajor Updates\n\"Aincrad 33F\" and a new quest has been implemented.\nAdded 33F boss avatars.\nThe super rare Gale Integral Series weapon transformation has been unlocked.\nAvatar Images\n《New Quest》\nMain Quest\nDragooning Factor\nStart Map\nHodge-Podge\nSub Quest\nStampede!\nStart NPC\nRoddy\nHarvest!\nStart NPC\nPotato Farmer Woman\nJust Normal Pigs\nStart NPC\nYoung Pig-Farming Man\nHoles in the Bug Net\nStart NPC\nShuntina\nCarrots Growing in the Desert\nStart NPC\nCoupli\nCharacter Quest\nLunching Factor 1\nStart Map\nMerchant District\nComrade\nSilica\nLunching Factor 2 [Eliminator Hunt]\nStart Map\nMerchant District\nComrade\nSilica\nTo unlock the subquest \"Holes in the Bug Net\", \"Carrots Growing in the Desert\" and Character Quest \"Lunching Factor 1\", complete the main quest on 33F.\n\"Lunching Factor 2 [Eliminator Hunt]\" will unlock after you complete \"Lunching Factor 1\"\nEliminator Armament Stones do not drop when you challenge \"Lunching Factor 2 [Eliminator Hunt]\" for the first time.\nEliminator Armament Stones drop from the multiple rounds of \"Lunching Factor 2 [Eliminator Hunt]\".\nThe drop rate for Gale Integral Series production and transformation materials is highest in Labyrinth - Interior.\nBoss Monster\nErak the Eliminator\nDetails\nSince this is a field with unusable items, some items cannot be used.\nSome attacks will remove buffs from the players.\nSome attacks will reduce the Awakening gauge.\nYou can break it with Dagger skills.\nSkill Breaks can be performed with skills that are both Slash Element and Earth Element.\nWith each Break or Skill Break, it will be weakened by a stack debuff that increases damage dealt from players.\nIt has a resistense that make it less susceptible to attacks with the Poison and Frostbite status ailments.\nIn the Character Quest and Labyrinth, at the beginning of battle, it grants a \"Critical resistance\" buff.\nIt uses the \"Seal item\" debuff.\nWeakness\nSlash Element\nEarth Element\nResistance\nThrust Element\nBlunt Element\nFire Element\nWater Element\nWind Element\nHoly Element\nDark Element\nPoison\nFrostbite\nCritical\nDamage\nCounter Switch Targeted Attacks\nYes\nBuffs used\nBuff \"Critical resistance\"\nStatus Ailments and Debuffs used\nStatus ailments \"Debility\", \"Fatal Poison\" and \"Stun\"\nDebuff \"Seal item\" and \"Decrease Defense\"\n* Break: Filling the entire Break Gauge will temporarily immobilize the boss and remove all of its buff effects.\n* Skill Break: By completely lowering the Skill Break Gauge, the boss will be temporarily immobilized and all of its buff effects will be removed.\nFor details on the effects of \"Status Ailments,\" please check in-game via \"Menu\" > \"System\" > \"Help\" > \"Buff, Debuff, and Status Ailments.\"\nAlternatively, please refer to the\n\"Status Ailments\"\nsection of the Play Guide.\n\"Gale Integral Series\" Transformations\n* Image is for visualization purposes only.\nThe super rare Gale Integral Series 3rd level weapon transformation has been unlocked!\nTransform the Gale Integral Series using Eliminator Armament Stones you collect!\nTransform to raise weapon stats and add special effects.\nHow to Transform to the 3rd Level\nSTEP1\nGet the Gale Integral Series to ★4 (2nd Level Transformation)!\nTransform \"Gale Integral Series\" to ★4 here.\nSTEP2\nUse the Stone+++ you produced and Eliminator Armament Stone to transform the Gale Integral Series to ★5!\nTo produce Stone+++, you will need the extremely rare Core Metal+++ and Stone+ materials that drop from the All Out Battle \"The Skull Reaper\" or All Out Battle [Aincrad].\n* Each \"Stone+++\" is associated with a different weapon type.\nExample: For 1H Swords or Daggers, you will need to produce Slicing Stone+++ using Core Metal+++ and Slicing Stone+.\nSTEP3\nUse the Stone+++ you produced and Eliminator Armament Stone to transform the Gale Integral Series to ★5!\nItems\nItem Icon\nItem Name\nEffect\nEliminator Armament Stone\nRare material from the 33F Erak the Eliminator. Use to produce or transform powerful weapons.\nCore Metal+++\nMaterial used to produce Stone+++.\nSlicing Stone+++\nSuperior material used to transform equipment.\nPiercing Stone+++\nSuperior material used to transform equipment.\nStriking Stone+++\nSuperior material used to transform equipment.\nGale Integral Series\nItem Icon\nItem Name\nType\n★5Capabilities\nGale Otius\n1H Sword\nAttack 2718\nGale Virtue\n1H Rapier\nAttack 2667\nGale Mudskipper\n1H Club\nAttack 2718\nGale El Nino\n2H Axe\nAttack 3213\nGale Lust\n2H Spear\nAttack 3154\nGale Tanngnidr\nBow\nAttack 3095\nGale Cadenza\nDagger\nAttack 2667\n* Values are based on maximum enhancement at ★5 rarity, Lv. 100.\nProducing Gale Integral Series Equipment\n\"Eliminator Armament Stone\" and \"Eliminator Waist Tie\" dropped by the 33F boss can be used to produce Gale Integral Series equipment.\n* The base statuses will not be different to Gale Integral Series equipment that can be produced on 23F and 19F.\n* Production recipes that use \"Eliminator Armament Stone\" and \"Eliminator Waist Tie\" will be available when you complete the 19F Main Quest.\nRandom Bonus\nThree types of one of the following will be randomly selected when producing the Gale Integral Series.\nStatus\n1H Sword/1H Rapier/1H Club/Bow/Dagger\n2H Axe/2H Spear\nAttack\n150\n300\nDefense\n50\n100\nHP\n2500\n5000\nExample: If three types of attacks are given to \"Gale El Nino\", attack will increase by 900 total.\n* A random bonus will be given.\n* Succession cannot be used.\nGo to Notice List"
