    "news_category": "UPDATE",
    "snippet": "새로운 런어웨이 플로어인 51층을 앞에 두고 어썰트 팀은 어찌할 바를 모르고 있었습니다. 51층은 과거 사악한 NPC들과 싸워 어썰트 팀에게 트라우마적인 상처를 남긴 범죄자들의 도시 피트(Pit)로 유명합니다. 설상가상으로 기소를 피한 오렌지 플레이어들은 하...",
    "full_details": "Notices\nNotice about Chapter 2 Aincrad 51F, super rare Machina Integral Series weapon, and other updates\nUPDATE\n2023-11-30 17:45:00\n（JST/GMT+9）\nThe Assault Team was at their wits' end in the face of the new Runaway Floor, the 51st.\nThe 51st floor is known for the Pit, a city of criminals that left traumatic scars on the Assault Team after their battles with wicked NPCs there in the past.\nWhat's worse, orange players who avoided prosecution have now gathered in the Pit from across the floors and grown merciless.\nHowever, in order to make it into the labyrinth, the Assault Team has no choice but to reconquer its streets that change so dizzyingly that some call them \"auto-generated,\" and so they decide to take emergency measures.\nMeanwhile, Vela's plans bring Leafa back together with Notte. While the interaction is awkward, they are able to connect once more.\nYet Vela's final moments continue to grow closer by the moment...\nMajor Updates\n\"Aincrad 51F\" and a new quest has been implemented.\nAdded 51F boss avatars.\nThe player level cap has been raised (Lv.230).\nThe Super rare \"Machina Integral Series\" of weapons has been added.\nFull Burst Skills added.\nDetails about the \"Full Burst Skill\" are available here\nRelaxed requirements on Integral Series production and transformation, as well as Chaos Showdown.\nRelaxed Requirement Details Here\nAvatar Images\n《New Quest》\nMain Quest\nLiving Factor\nStart NPC\nLower Pit\nSub Quest\nThe Dumb Get Kicked\nStart Map\nSketchy Man\nYou're the ****!\nStart Map\nGraffiti-Drawing Young Man\nBetter Than Getting Stabbed\nStart Map\nShady Wasp-Catcher\nBe Sharp, Not Round!\nStart Map\nPit Accessory Merchant\nMass-Produced Gear\nStart Map\nCreepy Man\nCharacter Quest\nCovering Factor 1\nStart NPC\nMerchant District\nComrade\nArgo\nCovering Factor 2 [Metal Reaper Hunt]\nStart NPC\nMerchant District\nComrade\nArgo\nUnlock the character quest \"Covering Factor 1\" by completing the 51F main quest.\n\"Covering Factor 2 [Metal Reaper Hunt] \" will unlock after you complete \"Covering Factor 1\"\nMetal Reaper Armament Stones do not drop when you challenge \"Covering Factor 2 [Metal Reaper Hunt] \" for the first time.\nMetal Reaper Armament Stones drop from the multiple rounds of \"Covering Factor 2 [Metal Reaper Hunt] \".\nThe drop rate for Machina Integral Series production materials is highest in Labyrinth - Interior.\nBoss Monster\nThe Metal Reaper\nDetails\nSince this is a field with unusable items, some items cannot be used.\nThe head, torso, tail, and several parts can be attacked, and a colored cursor will be displayed at the parts that can be attacked.\nThe damage it takes is constantly reduced, regardless of what part you attack.\nDamage to the torso is especially reduced.\nFor full-field attacks, as long as it is within range, damage will be dealt to all areas indicated with a colored cursor.\nOnly the following 3 types of Sword Skills can reduce the Skill Break gauge.\n①1H Club skills\n②2H Axe skills\n③Blunt element skills\nWhen a Skill Break happens, the boss will be temporarily immobilized and all its buffs will be removed.\nIn addition, when a Break happens, it will receive a stack debuff that\nincreases the damage it takes.\nAll skill breakable attacks can only reduce the Skill Break gauge when attacking the head.\nSome attacks will reduce the Awakening gauge.\nSome attacks will remove buffs from the players.\nWeakness\nBlunt Element\nEarth Element\nResistance\nSlash Element\nThrust Element\nFire Element\nWater Element\nWind Element\nHoly Element\nDark Element\nCritical\nDamage\nStatus Ailments\nBuffs used\nBuff \"Critical resistance\"\nStack Buff \"Increase Attack\" and \"Increase Defense\"\nStatus Ailments and Debuffs used\nStatus ailments \"Stun\" and \"Fatal Poison\"\nDebuff \"Seal item\"\n* Skill Break: By completely lowering the Skill Break Gauge, the boss will be temporarily immobilized and all of its buff effects will be removed.\nThe Machina Integral Series are special weapons added from 51F.\nThese are weapons that can be equipped from player level 221 with more attack powerful than any weapons before! (* At max enhancement)\nThe player level cap has also been raised from level 220 to level 230.\nMachina Integral Series\nItem Icon\nItem Name\nType\n★3Capabilities\nOtius\n1H Sword\nAttack 2343\nVirtue\n1H Rapier\nAttack 2300\nMudskipper\n1H Club\nAttack 2343\nEl Nino\n2H Axe\nAttack 2788\nLust\n2H Spear\nAttack 2737\nTanngnidr\nBow\nAttack 2686\nCadenza\nDagger\nAttack 2300\n* Values are based on maximum enhancement at ★3 rarity, Lv. 60.\nThe Machina Integral Series is planned to be evolvable in future updates and able to become even stronger.\nAfter production, go ahead and enhance them!\nMaterials required for production\nYou will need the \"Metal Reaper Armament Stone\" and the \"Metal Reaper Femur\" production materials that have an extremely rare chance of dropping from the 51F boss.\nRandom Bonus\nThree types of one of the following will be randomly selected when producing the Machina Integral Series.\nStatus\n1H Sword/1H Rapier/1H Club/Bow/Dagger\n2H Axe/2H Spear\nAttack\n125\n250\nDefense\n50\n100\nHP\n2500\n5000\nExample: If three types of attacks are given to \"El Nino\", attack will increase by 750 total.\n* A random bonus will be given.\n* Succession cannot be used.\nComparison with Gaou Integral Series\nType\nWeapon Name\nRarity\nEnhancement Level\nMax attack\n1H Sword\nGaou Astaroth\n★5\n100\n2290\nOtius\n★3\n60\n2343\n1H Rapier\nGaou Principality\n★5\n100\n2247\nVirtue\n★3\n60\n2300\n1H Club\nGaou Porcupine\n★5\n100\n2290\nMudskipper\n★3\n60\n2343\n2H Axe\nGaou Monsoon\n★5\n100\n2690\nEl Nino\n★3\n60\n2788\n2H Spear\nGaou Envy\n★5\n100\n2641\nLust\n★3\n60\n2737\nBow\nGaou Reginleifr\n★5\n100\n2591\nTanngnidr\n★3\n60\n2686\nDagger\nGaou Oratorio\n★5\n100\n2247\nCadenza\n★3\n60\n2300\nGo to Notice List"
